    "adHtml": "<h3>Remote, Philippines | Full-time contractor</h3>\n<h3>Who you are joining</h3>\n<p>Wunder Management is a European-led creator growth agency with a 25-person remote team. A large part of our team is based in the Philippines, including long-standing team members who have grown with the company and now own key parts of our operations.</p>\n<p>In the last three years, our content has generated more than 3 billion organic views across Instagram and TikTok. One of our biggest growth stories is taking a creator from around 5,000 to 700,000 Instagram followers.</p>\n<p>Wunder was founded by Lauris Kalnins, who is also an active content creator generating millions of organic views every month. You will join people who work inside social media every day—not a traditional agency watching from the outside.</p>\n<p>Lauris on Instagram: <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lauris_kalnins/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.instagram.com/lauris_kalnins/</a><br>Wunder Management: <a href=\"https://wundermgmt.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://wundermgmt.com/</a></p>\n<h3>Some of the creators we work with</h3>\n<p>Aya Rose: <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/itsayarose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.instagram.com/itsayarose</a><br>Katrina Zaiceva: <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/katrina.zaiceva\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.instagram.com/katrina.zaiceva</a><br>Sophie Jay: <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/justsophiejay/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.instagram.com/justsophiejay/</a></p>\n<h3>The role</h3>\n<p>We are hiring one person to own the day-to-day growth of a portfolio of around 8 creators.<br>This is not an assistant role. You will be the main person our creators speak with. Your job is to get content delivered, make each new piece better than the last, and keep creators moving when their motivation drops.</p>\n<h3>What you will own</h3>\n<ul><li>Manage the day-to-day relationship with your creator portfolio through calls and WhatsApp</li><li>Keep content delivery on track without waiting for someone else to remind you</li><li>Review Instagram and TikTok content and give clear, useful feedback</li><li>Study results with the creative team and help creators repeat what works</li><li>Lead a bigger one-to-one planning session with each creator during their lighter week each month</li><li>Turn those sessions into clear goals, actions and progress markers</li><li>Help creators solve routine account and payment questions using our internal AI guides</li><li>Keep complete notes so the team always knows what was agreed</li><li>Push firmly when someone falls behind while protecting a strong working relationship</li><li>Escalate serious account, relationship or delivery problems early</li></ul>\n<h3>How the work is divided</h3>\n<p>Around 90% of this role is Instagram growth: creator calls, content delivery, Reel feedback, testing and accountability.</p>\n<p>Our editing and chatting teams handle video editing, fan conversations and monetization. You coordinate with them so social growth, content and revenue stay aligned. You will not edit videos, publish content, create adult content or chat with fans.</p>\n<p>Our creators monetize through OnlyFans. You need to be comfortable working professionally in that business context, but it is not the focus of your daily work.</p>\n<h3>You should apply if</h3>\n<ul><li>You have at least three years of direct creator or social-media work</li><li>You have already managed creators, influencers or personal brands</li><li>You understand Instagram deeply and can explain why one Reel works better than another</li><li>You have served English-speaking clients across European, UK, Australian or US time zones</li><li>Your spoken and written English is excellent</li><li>You are organized, reliable and persistent with follow-ups</li><li>You can be warm with creators without becoming soft on delivery</li><li>You ask good questions and learn new systems quickly</li><li>You have stable internet and a real backup plan for internet or power problems</li></ul>\n<p>Direct creator-management experience is required.</p>\n<h3>Working hours</h3>\n<p>Your schedule must fully overlap with normal Riga working hours. In the Philippines, that is generally an afternoon-to-late-evening shift:</p>\n<ul><li>About 2:00 PM–11:00 PM during European summer time</li><li>About 3:00 PM–12:00 AM during European winter time</li><li>Half-day on Saturdays for creator calls, follow-ups and planning</li><li>Sunday off, apart from rare urgent problems</li></ul>\n<p>The exact daily schedule will be agreed before you start.<br>Expect roughly 44 working hours each week, plus normal breaks.</p>\n<h3>Compensation</h3>\n<ul><li>$1,500 USD fixed monthly contractor fee</li><li>Up to $1,000 USD monthly performance bonus under the agreed bonus policy</li><li>Full-time, exclusive contractor agreement</li></ul>\n<p>The fixed fee is guaranteed under the contract. The bonus is earned, not automatic. Exceptional performance can take total monthly compensation to $2,500 USD.<br>This is a contractor role, not Philippine employment. You are responsible for your own taxes and government benefits.</p>\n<h3>Hiring process</h3>\n<ol><li>First interview with our operations team</li><li>Final interview with the founder</li><li>Paid three-day trial</li></ol>\n<h3>The trial is simple:</h3>\n<ul><li>Day 1: Learn and shadow</li><li>Day 2: Complete basic tasks</li><li>Day 3: Do real work with smaller creator accounts</li></ul>\n<p>We do not expect perfection after three days. We do expect fast learning, useful questions, strong follow-up and clear value.</p>",
